  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Stenopalustroside B and the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype, as both entities are linked through a series of molecular interactions. Stenopalustroside B is identified as a target of CWR22R, which in turn is a target of Baptifoline. Additionally, CWR22R is a target of another compound, which ultimately targets the EP4 subtype of the prostaglandin receptor. This indicates a possible pathway where Stenopalustroside B may influence the EP4 receptor through CWR22R, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The scores assigned to these relationships suggest a moderate level of confidence in the proposed connections, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the functional relevance of this interaction.",
